  {
   "rule": "This is a <strong>verbal sentence</strong>: the verb usually comes first, then the doer (<em>fāʿil</em>), which is <span class='ar raf'>marfūʿ</span>: <span class='ar'>ذَهَبَ</span> <span class='ar raf'>مُحَمَّدٌ</span>. The basic past form <span class='ar'>ذَهَبَ</span> already means “he went”. If no doer is named, “he” is understood."
  },
